<title>JAPAN: S.Korea Cheju Island launches 3.05% samurai-Nomura.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Cheju Island launches 3.05% samurai-Nomura.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following samurai bond issue was announced by lead-manager Nomura Securities on Tuesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  South Korea's Cheju Island</p>
<p> AMT		 20 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.05 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  4 July 2007</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  4 July 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	June 30 to July 2</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     JBRI AA+</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
